  "review_scope": "An additive physical formulation of Theorem 2 with arbitrary isometric tensor and PRV realizations, existence witnesses, and a separately redeclared state/channel challenge. The original four endpoint types and all baseline production modules are retained exactly.",
  "remaining_shared_boundary": "The lower representation models, index spaces, generator actions, and numerical definitions remain shared; see metadata/physical-interface-map.json. This record does not establish independent human correspondence review.",
  "policy": "Bindings preserve the source/report history and support a bounded additive agent review. Freshness validation does not itself rerun proof checkers or decide mathematical meaning. Historical source-first reviews retain their original dates, provenance and scope.",
  "reviewed_at_utc": "2026-10-09T03:20:31.034906+00:00",
  "reviewers": [
    {
      "id": "/root/independent_spec_review",
      "role": "Separate final source review of state/projector bridges, expected types, realization existence, and compiled-closure guard; also contributed earlier expected-fixture tooling. This is agent review, not blind or human review."
    },
    {
      "id": "/root/independent_projector",
      "role": "Additive source preservation and original compiled-endpoint hash review; contributed forward projector uniqueness."
    },
    {
      "id": "/root",
      "role": "Integration and execution of fresh production, statement, Comparator and Nanoda checks."
    }
  ],
  "review_findings": [
    "No state-identification or projector-equality premise is supplied; the bridges derive these equalities from literal isometry and intertwining conditions.",
    "The existence root constructs both physical tensor embeddings and both forward/reverse PRV realizations for every admissible pair, independently of the unitary parameter.",
    "The three raw definitions and the two expected theorem signatures match the solution at source level; exported statement comparison and kernel runs are recorded separately.",
    "The reverse intertwining condition uses the dual auxiliary generator representation.",
    "The lower representation coordinates/generators and numerical expressions remain shared. No independent human correspondence review is established."
  ]
}
